invariant: INV-16
file: src/mldsa_neon.c
catches: test/docker-aes-runtime-qemu.sh keccak
reason: an arm64 host object samples the seventh entry of each row of A
  through the call that takes no value. So key generation, a signature and
  a verification under CH_CPU_CONSTANT_TIME_SHA3 run eight SHAKE128
  streams of ExpandA on sha3.c. Every key, signature and verdict stays
  right, so no vector notices. bin/mldsa_runtime_test counts each SHAKE
  call on each path under every ch_cfg.cpu value. The first six entries of
  a row run on the two-way Keccak, and INV-69's violations hold them.
  mldsa.c's and mldsa_sign_steps.c's own loops run in no arm64 host
  object, because mld_wide_runs returns 1 there (docs/decisions.md 198).
  Only an arm64 object that clang compiled has the instructions' path, so
  the script builds the binary with clang for arm64 and runs it under
  qemu-aarch64.

--- old
        return mld_sample_ntt_cpu(cpu, &e[0], rho, (uint8_t)first, (uint8_t)i);
--- new
        return mld_sample_ntt(&e[0], rho, (uint8_t)first, (uint8_t)i);
